WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.567
-Welcome back.
It is always great to see you.

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:04.834
Thank you for taking some time
to say hi to us.

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:06.400
Congrats on the new album,
by the way.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.334
You just dropped this.

00:00:07.334 --> 00:00:11.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.901
Crushed it with this.

00:00:12.901 --> 00:00:14.167
No one knew it was going to
come out.

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:16.033
I guess you knew
it was going to come out.

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:17.734
-Obviously.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:19.067
How long ago did you know, like,

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:20.067
"Oh, yeah,
I'm going to release this"?

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:22.901
-Um...
[ Speaking Spanish ]

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:25.167
Since I started to work on it.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:28.133
-Yeah -- Yeah, that's true.
I understand that.

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.934
But to come out now,
I know you like to give little

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:32.901
Easter eggs
and hints to your fans.

00:00:32.901 --> 00:00:34.801
But you, like, just dropped it
out of nowhere.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.834
-Yeah, well, they already know.

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:39.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:42.701
-What does the title mean again?

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:44.567
-"Nadie sabe lo que va
a pasar mañana," that means

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:47.801
like nobody knows what is going
to happen tomorrow.

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:49.767
I guess you know.
[ Cheers ]

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:50.968
-Nobody knows
what's going to happen tomorrow.

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:52.501
-Yeah, nobody knows.

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:53.868
-It became the most
streamed album

00:00:53.868 --> 00:00:56.501
in a single day
this year on Spotify.

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:57.868
It's already breaking
all these records.

00:00:57.868 --> 00:00:58.934
Congratulations.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:00.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:03.200
[ Speaking Spanish ]

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.567
-It's great. It is so great.
-Feels good.

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:07.467
-22 tracks.
It's unbelievable.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.467
You had a listening party
in Puerto Rico

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:10.968
and here's your entrance.

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:12.334
16,000 people.

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:15.834
You entered -- You came from
the roof in a Rolls Royce.

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:18.334
I mean, being lowered
from the ceiling.

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:19.701
Were you scared at all?

00:01:19.701 --> 00:01:22.767
-[ Speaking Spanish ]
A little bit, yeah.

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:24.334
But I had fun. It was --

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:26.334
-You always do fun things,
by the way.

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:27.567
-Yeah.
-I know I saw the video

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:30.434
from Monaco, you had
a special guest with you.

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:33.367
-Who's that?
-I'm talking about Al Pacino.

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:37.334
-Aw, look.
-Yeah, not too shabby, bud.

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:41.467
You and Al Pacino --
you even included

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:43.868
a little moment in this video
which I want to show everyone.

00:01:43.868 --> 00:01:45.200
Just a little piece.
Can we take a look at this?

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.067
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:50.501
How's it going?
-Playing games.

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:51.901
What else is new?

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:53.467
Hey, you're doing great.
-Thank you.

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:54.901
-You really are doing great.

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:57.067
He's charging it up.

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:58.300
They wrote a song.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:03.067
♪ You never know
what tomorrow brings ♪

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:04.434
-[ Vocalizes ]

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:09.434
-♪ Never know what tomorrow
takes from you ♪

00:02:09.434 --> 00:02:11.200
-I mean, come on.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.634
That's Al Pacino.

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:16.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
How cool is that?

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.968
-That was amazing.

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:21.033
That was a great experience
working with Al Pacino.

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:22.200
That was very exciting.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.767
-How did you get hooked up
with Al Pacino?

00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:27.200
-Well, I don't even know
if people know,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.100
Al Pacino is my uncle.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.033
-Oh, my gosh.
I didn't know that.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:33.234
That's amazing.
I didn't know that at all.

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:36.300
-[ Speaking Spanish ]
No.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.300
Actually, I don't know
how we connect with him.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.567
But --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.567 --> 00:02:43.334
I'm very grateful 'cause
that was a dream come true.

00:02:43.334 --> 00:02:45.033
-Yeah. He's a legend.

00:02:45.033 --> 00:02:45.868
He's the best.
-He's a legend.

00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:47.567
I love his movies.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:49.667
"Scarface", "Godfather",
"Carlito's Way."

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:51.367
I love him.
-Yeah, everything he does --

00:02:51.367 --> 00:02:54.167
-It was just
a very special day for me.

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:56.434
-You just released that you
have -- this afternoon,

00:02:56.434 --> 00:02:58.834
actually, you announced that
you're going on tour again.

00:02:58.834 --> 00:02:59.934
-I did?
-Yes.

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:01.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
You have to.

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:03.100
Yes.
-Are you sure?

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:06.300
-Yes. It's happening this next
year, I think, in February.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.667
Yeah, you'll be --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:10.834
All over North America.

00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:14.400
-Yes, I'm very happy.
-But isn't that work for you?

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:18.300
Isn't that like -- Do you like
performing and going on tour?

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.968
-I love perform-- Yeah,
of course I love performing.

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:24.501
It's my -- I think -- I love
to create at the studio.

00:03:24.501 --> 00:03:28.567
But I think to perform
to the people

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:31.601
is my favorite thing
about the music.

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:35.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Like, what part?

00:03:35.934 --> 00:03:38.033
Is it when people sing
the song back to you?

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.133
-Yes.

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:42.100
I think that's the best
feeling ever.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:48.801
Like --
[ Speaking Spanish ]

00:03:48.801 --> 00:03:50.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:52.300
And I missed it.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:55.300
I missed it.
-Yeah, we need you, bud.

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:56.534
It's great.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:58.567
You know, since we've known
each other,

00:03:58.567 --> 00:04:00.968
you just watched your career
just go skyrocketing.

00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:02.868
It's awesome.
I'm so happy for you.

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:08.100
There's actually college courses
teaching about you at colleges.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:11.300
"Bad Bunny, race, gender,
empire, and reggaeton"

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:12.901
at Wellesley College.

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:15.100
"Bad Bunny and resistance"
in Puerto Rico"

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.167
is Loyola Marymount University.

00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:20.100
Did you ever think
you were going to be taught --

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.033
a course at a school?
-Noooooo.

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:23.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.801 --> 00:04:25.734
No.
-Is that cool?

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:28.634
-That's a very crazy thing.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:32.834
I'm still --
[ Speaking Spanish ]

00:04:32.834 --> 00:04:35.901
Sometimes people came to me
like,

00:04:35.901 --> 00:04:37.367
"Yeah, I'm taking this class
about you."

00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:40.834
I'm like, "What? Really?"

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:43.501
I don't know.
Feels weird.

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:48.634
But I would love to take
one of those classes.

00:04:48.634 --> 00:04:50.901
[ Laughter ]
-You'll be really good.

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:56.033
-I think I would get an A.

00:04:56.033 --> 00:04:57.634
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
You would ace that.

00:04:57.634 --> 00:04:59.334
You would get an A
in that course.

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:00.567
-[ Speaking Spanish ]

00:05:00.567 --> 00:05:02.200
-You know everything about
Bad Bunny.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.033
Absolutely, yeah.

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:05.634
I didn't get a chance
to tell you

00:05:05.634 --> 00:05:07.367
how great you were
at the Grammys, by the way.

00:05:07.367 --> 00:05:08.767
This is you.

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:11.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:14.968
Before you won your third
Grammy, congratulations.

00:05:14.968 --> 00:05:16.334
-Thank you.
-But I heard that this

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:18.567
wasn't supposed to be
the opening of the Grammys.

00:05:18.567 --> 00:05:19.934
Is that true?
-That's true.

00:05:19.934 --> 00:05:22.400
How you know that?
-Because I do research.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:23.934
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.934 --> 00:05:25.734
-Al Pacino is my uncle.

00:05:25.734 --> 00:05:28.300
[ Laughter ]
-That's true, that's true.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.601
It wasn't supposed to be
the opening act.

00:05:30.601 --> 00:05:32.067
But I think -- I don't know.

00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:37.667
I guess the producer saw it
at the rehearsal.

00:05:37.667 --> 00:05:40.601
And he said like, "This is
the best thing about the night."

00:05:40.601 --> 00:05:47.701
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:05:47.701 --> 00:05:51.200
-When you do those shows,
awards shows, like do you get --

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:52.934
is it a little bit
different crowd because you see

00:05:52.934 --> 00:05:56.200
like Taylor Swift
and Jack Harlow dancing to you?

00:05:56.200 --> 00:06:00.801
-I don't care.
Like, it's fine.

00:06:00.801 --> 00:06:01.834
-It's fine. It's the same.

00:06:01.834 --> 00:06:03.267
But is that the same
as when you --

00:06:03.267 --> 00:06:06.234
-It's the same. Taylor likes
to dance to everybody's music.

00:06:06.234 --> 00:06:07.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:09.767
So, I know she's gonna be
like be --

00:06:09.767 --> 00:06:11.634
And --
-She'll be there for you, yeah.

00:06:11.634 --> 00:06:13.534
And she'll be moving
around for you.

00:06:13.534 --> 00:06:14.868
But when you do that
or when you did

00:06:14.868 --> 00:06:16.534
Yankee Stadium, by the way.

00:06:16.534 --> 00:06:20.634
Did you --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:20.634 --> 00:06:22.667
-I preferred
Yankee Stadium, of course.

00:06:22.667 --> 00:06:25.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.734
-How'd that feel?
-That was another --

00:06:27.734 --> 00:06:31.767
a very special day in my life
'cause New York

00:06:31.767 --> 00:06:35.334
always feels, like, special,
feels like home.

00:06:35.334 --> 00:06:38.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:38.667 --> 00:06:41.667
Yeah. Like, it's weird.

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:47.434
It's something very special
being far from Puerto Rico

00:06:47.434 --> 00:06:49.367
but it feels like
you are in home.

00:06:49.367 --> 00:06:52.234
There's a lot of Puerto Rican,
there's a lot of Dominicans.

00:06:52.234 --> 00:06:53.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:53.567 --> 00:06:56.234
[ Speaking Spanish ]

00:06:56.234 --> 00:07:01.367
So every New York show is
a very special show to me,

00:07:01.367 --> 00:07:04.634
and the New York Yankee Stadium
was something

00:07:04.634 --> 00:07:05.901
that I'm never going to forget.
-Two sold-out shows,

00:07:05.901 --> 00:07:07.634
not too shabby, bud.

00:07:07.634 --> 00:07:10.467
And now you're taking part of
another iconic part of New York.

00:07:10.467 --> 00:07:13.501
You're hosting and musical guest
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:07:13.501 --> 00:07:15.000
Double duty. Double whammy.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:16.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:16.234 --> 00:07:19.200
Double down. Double down.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.868
Man, that's a lot of work!

00:07:21.868 --> 00:07:23.434
It's a lot of work.

00:07:23.434 --> 00:07:24.701
How does it feel, though,
going in?

00:07:24.701 --> 00:07:26.300
You got some funny sketches?

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.534
-Yeah, yeah.

00:07:27.534 --> 00:07:29.133
[ Laughter ]

00:07:29.133 --> 00:07:30.234
But I need to sleep.

00:07:30.234 --> 00:07:31.601
[ Laughter ]

00:07:31.601 --> 00:07:34.234
-No. No, this is when you have
to just stay awake.

00:07:34.234 --> 00:07:36.067
Because that's the whole
secret of "Saturday Night Live."

00:07:36.067 --> 00:07:38.000
Like, when I was on that show,
I never --

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.601
I went to bed every night
at probably 3:00 in the morning,

00:07:40.601 --> 00:07:43.801
just so when it's 11:30,
I'm like ready to go.

00:07:43.801 --> 00:07:45.000
I would sleep during
the day, man.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:46.067
It was crazy.
-Nah, it's crazy.

00:07:46.067 --> 00:07:49.000
But I've been
enjoying the process.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:52.200
All the cast, the producers,
the writers.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:56.467
The vibe is a very cool vibe
so I'm grateful.

00:07:56.467 --> 00:07:59.033
And I'm very excited
about this Saturday.

00:07:59.033 --> 00:08:01.100
This Saturday?
-Yeah, this Saturday.

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:02.767
Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:02.767 --> 00:08:04.667
We're already getting
the word down that

00:08:04.667 --> 00:08:06.567
everyone loves you up there.
And you're just like,

00:08:06.567 --> 00:08:08.000
"Dude, he's the nicest guy."

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.167
Everyone's freaking out.

00:08:09.167 --> 00:08:10.467
And they're like,
"It's a great, funny show."

00:08:10.467 --> 00:08:11.868
So, congrats.
We'll all be watching.

00:08:11.868 --> 00:08:14.167
-[ Speaking Spanish ]
-No, it'll be great.

00:08:14.167 --> 00:08:16.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
We'll be watching Bad Bunny.

00:08:16.367 --> 00:08:18.601
Check him out on
"Saturday Night Live."

00:08:18.601 --> 00:08:20.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:20.334 --> 00:08:24.067
This weekend,
the host and musical guest.

00:08:24.067 --> 00:08:26.133
We'll be right back
with Charli D'Amelio.

00:08:26.133 --> 00:08:27.801
Stick around, everybody!

